# Shell scripts must keep Unix line endings.
#
# Git on Windows converts checked-out files to CRLF by default. A shell script
# with CRLF fails on Linux at its first loop or conditional:
#
#   syntax error near unexpected token $'do\r'
#
# which reads like a broken script rather than a line-ending problem. These are
# the deployment scripts, so the failure would land on a fresh server, at the
# worst moment, on someone's first attempt.
*.sh text eol=lf

# Same reasoning for anything else read by a Linux tool rather than an editor.
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf

# Let git handle the rest normally.
* text=auto
